    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d555">

                <pb facs="0499" n="383" xml:id="pg383"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 738.3915/112a.]</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the
                            Dominican Minister.</hi><anchor n="1"
                        xml:id="d555-f1"/>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1912-04-26">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">April 26, 1912</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">My Dear Mr. Minister</hi>: In view of the fact that
                    the Minister of Haiti is now in receipt of new full powers to negotiate
                    concerning the Dominican-Haitian boundary dispute, I should be glad to have the
                    plenipotentiaries meet at the Department of State at 10 o’clock Saturday
                    morning, April 27th, for the purpose of renewing active negotiations, and I
                    shall be happy to be present at the meeting.</p>
                <p>I have informed the Minister of Haiti in like sense.</p>
                <p>I am [etc.].</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">P. C. Knox.</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d555-f1" n="1" type="source" xml:id="d555-f1-content">
                <p>The same, mutatis mutandis, to the Haitian Minister.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
